{"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4410743092":"Motion Industries is seeking a Software Developer to perform basic problem resolution analysis and corrections, develop new software based on approved design documents, and correct system problems. We offer an excellent benefits package that includes a 401(k) plan, healthcare coverage, tuition reimbursement, vacation, sick, and holiday pay.\n   \n\n  \n\n You must be eligible to work in the US without Visa Sponsorship.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Develop software applications based on approved design\n* Perform basic problem resolution analysis and correction\n* Correct system problems as directed by manager\n* Ensure projects are delivered on time and according to specifications\n* Use standard coding techniques to ensure application performance meets requirements\n* Work as part of a team for most projects\n\n\n**Qualifications**\n* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems or related field or equivalent work experience\n* Experience with structured application development and change control methodologies\n* Experience with object oriented analysis and design\n* Good knowledge of database design, programming languages and coding techniques\n\n\n Not the right fit? Let us know you're interested in a future opportunity by joining our Talent Community on jobs.genpt.com or create an account to set up email alerts as new job postings become available that meet your interest!\n   \n\n  \n\n GPC conducts its business without regard to sex, race, creed, color, religion, marital status, national origin, citizenship status, age, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, disability, military status, status as a veteran, or any other protected characteristic. GPC's policy is to recruit, hire, train, promote, assign, transfer and terminate employees based on their own ability, achievement, experience and conduct and other legitimate business reasons.","https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/wovencare/jobs/5438348008":"Passing your boards is a big deal. Where you take your first BCBA role is an equally big deal, because the environment you start in shapes the kind of clinician you become. Finding the right place to do it really matters!\nAt Woven Care, we are a pediatric outpatient practice dedicated to helping children and families thrive. We have built a new BCBA experience around what we know matters most: a manageable caseload, genuine clinical support, and a multidisciplinary team that is invested in growing together.\nWhat Your First Year Looks Like Here\nThis is the next chapter in your clinical journey, and you won't be navigating it alone. From day one you'll be surrounded by BCBAs and colleague in OT, PT, and SLP who love what they do and are excited to collaborate and grow alongside you.\nOnboarding is thoughtfully designed with dedicated support and mentorship woven in from the start, ramping your caseload gradually so you can build confidence and clinical depth at the same time. You will carry up to a 10-client caseload sized so you can do your best work rather than just manage volume.\nDay to day, you can expect to design and guide ABA programs, conduct assessments, supervise and mentor your RBT team, lead parent training sessions, and collaborate directly with your multidisciplinary team on shared clients. Documentation flexibility means as long as your job responsibilities are met, you can handle notes and indirect tasks from home, so your clinic time stays focused on what matters most: the kids and families you serve.\nWhat You'll Get at Woven Care\nA team that's here for YOU\nYour clinical team is readily available and invested in your growth and where you are on your journey. From programming questions to caregiver communication and RBT supervision challenges, support is by your side. Plus, our multidisciplinary model means you'll collaborate daily with Speech, OT, and PT, gaining new perspectives and building a richer understanding of every child you serve. You'll never feel alone at Woven Care!\nLearning opportunities right from the start\nWe want to build a team of BCBAs who never stop learning; that's why we've created a program that prioritizes professional growth throughout your career. You'll have access to:\n$250 CEU reimbursement,  increasing up to $1,500 annually with tenure\nIn-house CEU opportunities and ongoing clinical guidance built into how we operate\nCompensation\nNew BCBAs receive a salary compensation range of $78,000–$82,000/year. Plus, we have a monthly productivity bonus of up to $750 ($9,000 annually).\nSign-on bonus\nUp to $10,000 in bonus pay. Whether you're relocating or just starting strong, we want to help you get here!\nBenefits options\nMedical, dental, vision, tenure-based PTO, and sick leave accruing 128 hours your first year, six guaranteed holidays, life and disability insurance, and 401(k) with match after 1 year!\nWhat You'll Need\nCurrent BCBA certification in good standing\nNew BCBAs welcome!\nCompensation and Benefit Information\nComp and Benefits\n$78,000 — $82,000 USD\nEqual Employment Opportunity:  We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, or any other status protected by law. Woven Care uses e-Verify to authorize eligibility for employment."}
