 We're building the infrastructure that helps an entire industry move faster, reach more people, and deliver on its promise.\n\nBacked by leading investors (Goldman Sachs, Hedosophia, NEA, Valar, 8VC) and trusted by major carriers, Bestow is powered by a team that moves with precision, purpose, and heart. If you want to help reimagine a centuries-old industry with lasting impact, join us.\n\nBestow offers flexible remote/hybrid work, meaningful benefits, equity, and substantial growth opportunities.\n\nBestow uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit E-Verify.gov http://e-verify.gov.\n\nAbout the Team — Pre-Sales Tools\n\nPre-Sales Tools powers tools and experiences letting insurance agents and distribution partners quote, configure, submit applications before checkout. It's Bestow's B2B front door — if agents struggle here, they send leads elsewhere. Team has 8 engineers.\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\n - Build and scale Go services powering agent quoting, configuration, application-submission tools used before checkout\n\n - Partner closely w/ App & Checkout teams given tight coupling between surfaces\n\n - Resolve partner-specific edge cases as distribution partners and volume scale\n\n - Write unit and integration tests for code you ship; peer review code from others on team\n\n - Use AI coding tools (Copilot, Claude Code, Cursor, etc.) as default part of daily workflow — expectation, not bonus skill\n\n - Support knowledge transfer to team with high contractor ratio (Howdy), pairing and documenting as you go\n\n - Follow and help improve automation, CI/CD practices across team\n\nWho You Are\n\n - 3+ years professional backend software development experience\n\n - Professional experience with Go; comfortable owning services end to end\n\n - Experience with distributed systems or microservices, and designing APIs (REST, gRPC, OpenAPI, Protocol Buffers)\n\n - Experience using Docker for local development, and CI/CD as default practice\n\n - Demonstrated, day-to-day fluency using AI tools (Copilot, Claude Code, Cursor, ChatGPT, etc.) in real engineering work — able to speak concretely about where they help and where they don't\n\n - Comfortable contributing to architectural discussions and picking up mentorship moments as they come, even without a formal title\n\nCompetencies\n\n - Go Backend Craftsmanship: Writes idiomatic, maintainable Go services; understands concurrency, error handling, package structure well enough to keep code healthy as it scales\n\n - System Design & Architecture: Designs components that hold up under growth, stay maintainable, fit Bestow's existing platform rather than fighting it\n\n - API Design: Designs clear, versioned APIs (REST/gRPC/OpenAPI) that internal teams and, where relevant, distribution partners can consume without guesswork\n\n - Testing & Quality Discipline: Writes unit and integration tests as default habit, not afterthought; catches edge cases before they reach production\n\n - AI-Augmented Engineering: Uses AI tools (Copilot, Claude Code, Cursor, ChatGPT, etc.) as default part of daily engineering work — for code, tests, debugging, or design — while applying independent technical judgment to output\n\n - Cross-Team Collaboration: Works effectively across tightly coupled teams and partners, especially App & Checkout\n\n - Debugging & Production Support: Diagnoses and resolves issues in previously delivered features methodically, under real production constraints\n\n - Communication Clarity: Explains technical tradeoffs in language that fits audience — engineers, PMs, non-technical partners\n\n - Growth & Collaboration:\n\n\nTOTAL REWARDS\n\nAt Bestow, we’re proud to be awarded for our team members, innovative products, and culture. Our standard benefits for full-time employees include:\n\n - Competitive salary and equity based on role\n\n - Policies and managers that support work/life balance, like our flexible paid time off and parental leave programs\n\n - 100% paid-premium option for medical, dental, and vision insurance\n\n - Lifestyle stipend to support your physical, emotional, and financial wellbeing\n\n - Flexible work-from-home policy and open to remote\n\n - Remote and WFH options, as well as a beautiful, state-of-the-art office in Dallas’ Deep Ellum, for those who prefer an office setting\n\n - Employee-led diversity, equity, and inclusion initiatives\n\nRecent Employer Awards include:\n\n - Best Place for Working Parents 2023 + 2024 + 2025\n\n - Great Place to Work Certified, 2022 + 2023 + 2024 + 2025\n\n - Built In Best Places to Work, 2022 + 2023 + 2025\n\n - Fortune’s Best Workplaces in Texas 2022 + 2023\n\n - Fortune’s Best Workplaces in Financial Services and Insurance 2022 + 2023 + 2024\n\nWe value diversity at Bestow. The company will hire, recruit, and promote regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, pregnancy or maternity, veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable law. We understand the importance of creating a safe and comfortable work environment and encourage individualism and authenticity in every team member.\n\nThanks for considering a job at Bestow!","https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/brunswickgroup/jobs/8821383002":"AI Engineer\nOpportunity\nBrunswick is on an exciting journey to harness the power of artificial intelligence and data science to enhance the way we work and the advice we provide to clients. As we continue to expand our AI capabilities, we are looking for an AI Engineer to join our growing team.\nIn this role, you will be responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining AI-powered applications that deliver real value across the business. Working closely with our existing AI team, you will help build innovative solutions using modern AI technologies, with a particular focus on large language models (LLMs).\nThis is an excellent opportunity for someone with hands-on experience developing and deploying AI applications who enjoys solving complex problems, working with a high degree of autonomy, and turning emerging technologies into practical, high-quality products.\nYou will thrive in this role if you are curious, creative, and passionate about applying AI to solve real-world business challenges. You take pride in writing robust, maintainable code and enjoy collaborating with colleagues to continuously improve and expand our AI capabilities.\nAbout the Role\nYour day-to-day responsibilities will include:\nSupport, run, and iterate existing AI applications.\nDesign, develop, deploy, and maintain new AI applications which can be scaled across multiple business use cases, driving operational and commercial outcomes.\nTrial and test solutions with end users to iterate and optimize them.\nResearch and analyze data sets using a variety of statistical and machine learning techniques.\nTrack and understand the evolving AI landscape.\nWhat We're Looking For\nThe successful candidate will be a highly professional, well-rounded individual with strong problem-solving skills, engineering expertise, strategic thinking, and excellent interpersonal skills. They will have a strong academic background complemented by an outstanding career to date. Standout candidates will demonstrate:\nExperience building solutions with large language models (LLMs) and a deep understanding of the broader generative AI landscape.\nExperience designing datasets, conducting model evaluations, and fine-tuning foundation models to improve task-specific performance.\nStrong Python development skills, including experience writing production-quality code.\nExperience with front-end technologies such as JavaScript, React, HTML, and CSS.\nA solid understanding of statistics and machine learning fundamentals.\nAn undergraduate degree in a quantitative discipline, such as Mathematics or Computer Science, or equivalent relevant industry experience.\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to communicate technical concepts effectively to both technical and non-technical audiences.\nThe ability to thrive in a fast-paced, evolving environment with changing priorities and an iterative, user-focused approach to development.\nCuriosity, a strong sense of ownership, and the ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively.\nPrevious experience in professional services would be advantageous.\nExperience developing cloud applications on Microsoft Azure would be advantageous.\nExperience with DevOps practices and tools (e.g. CI/CD, Git) would be desirable.\nKnowledge of, or experience with, secure software development practices would be advantageous.\nWhy Join Us\nWhether you are joining a client facing team, a core services team, or starting out on your professional career journey, joining Brunswick unlocks a range of employee benefits to support your financial future, health and wellness, family and community and continuous professional development.\nThe successful applicant will be eligible for the following compensation and benefits package:\nBase Pay: The annual base compensation range for this role is $130,000 - $180,000 . The base pay offered will be determined by factors including experience, skills, training, office location, certifications, and education.\nBonus Eligibility: Annual discretionary bonus contingent upon individual and firm-wide performance.\nBenefits: Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance. Disability insurance. Employee assistance program. Flexible spending account. Health savings account. Life insurance. Commuter Benefits. Generous Paid Time Off: 25 vacation days and 10 days sick leave, as well as 11 paid company holidays. Firm-sponsored 401(k) Plan with 3% automatic company contribution of base and bonus with an additional 1.5% profit share– immediate vesting. Career training and development opportunities. Employee discounts.\nOffice Policy: At Brunswick, our work is a craft that thrives in teaching environments – whether in our offices or on-site with clients – through real-time observation, collaboration, human connection, clear guidance and by challenging one another to keep getting better. Our policy is that our team members are in person – either in the office or on-site with clients – at least four days each week.\nThe firm will provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants or employees, as defined by applicable law. In addition to the application, the process may include virtual and in-person interviews, as well as an assessment, which may be timed. To request an accommodation during our application and hiring process, email americasaccommodations@brunswickgroup.com .\nAbout Brunswick\nBrunswick is a global advisory firm. We help companies tackle high-stakes issues, navigate complex stakeholder relationships, and deliver high-impact outcomes.\nOur clients value our ability to anticipate, shape, and respond to the key players and forces in the financial and investment arena, regulatory and geopolitical universe, NGO community, workforce and beyond. They rely on us for deep experience, fresh perspectives and original thinking. So, in Brunswick you will find an exceptional range of experience and talent with a rich mix of backgrounds. From the beginning, we have prioritized attracting, developing, and retaining the best professionals in the industry, united by a culture of inclusivity, excellence, and intellectual curiosity.\nFounded in 1987 in London, the firm has organically grown to 27 offices in 18 countries across the Americas, Europe, Middle East, Africa, Asia and Australia. We operate as a “one-firm firm” with no individual profit centers. This allows us to assemble fully integrated, bespoke teams for each client, able to draw on the full resources of Brunswick anywhere in the world.\nBrunswick is an equal opportunity employer.  All qualified applicants will be considered without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, disability, pregnancy, genetic information, or any other status protected by applicable law. Please read our Global Privacy Notice to understand how your data is managed."}
